{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_eSc87xXMgdHKGARGDn45opAf","content":"## hardening3-h3-1...origin/hardening3-h3-1\n?? BRIEF-h3-1-fix.md\n?? BRIEF-h3-1.md\n?? BRIEF-wedge.md\n?? REVIEW-d2-revise2.diff\n?? REVIEW-d2.diff\n?? REVIEW-h3-1-fix.diff\nc3163fb51 (HEAD -> hardening3-h3-1, origin/hardening3-h3-1) test(latte): H3-1 wedge round 2 — the encoder-layer theory retracted; the stall is kernel-attempt's evidence walk over the exhausted :consumer machine\n8ea857c13 test(latte): the H3-1 wedge diagnostic — the semantic evaluator terminates; the wedge lives in the encoder session layer\na8980db83 docs(latte): H3-2 fixture-family preparation — the proof-elaboration family designed and A-verified\n805d81d65 wip(hardening3): D2 token-packet lane + packet arity guard + adversarial regression — reference-only, pending the semantic-lane wall-clock report\nc3163fb5 test(latte): H3-1 wedge round 2 — the encoder-layer theory retracted; the stall is kernel-attempt's evidence walk over the exhausted :consumer machine\n ...-engineer-h3-1-wedge-round2.glm-5.3.findings.md | 264 +++++++++\n .../1794100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.minrepro.log |  40 ++\n ...4100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-gate1.log | 556 +++++++++++++++++++\n ...94100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-run1.log |  12 +\n ...00000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-walker1.log |  10 +\n ...0000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-walker8m.log |  10 +\n test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj                        | 280 ++++++++++\n test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj                           | 592 +++++++++++++++++++++\n 8 files changed, 1764 insertions(+)\n"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_T6TmVh30cP4Ksq7XVJir3jUN","content":"1\t(ns d2-wedge-min-repro\n2\t  \"The minimized reproduction of the H3-1 'wedge' — which is a false\n3\t  negative, not a cycle.\n4\t\n5\t  What round 1 measured as 'the evaluator session terminates': a probe that\n6\t  built `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session` and called\n7\t  `observer/run-on-stream` — but never appended the fixture to the session\n8\t  medium (no `tu/queue-rows!`). An observer session over an empty medium\n9\t  loads nothing and runs nothing, and a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true`\n10\t  before any program (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm mints `:halted? true`), so\n11\t  the probe read 'halted, zero budget spent' off a machine that never\n12\t  executed an instruction.\n13\t\n14\t  This file is the A/B/C pair that isolates it, each arm runnable alone:\n15\t\n16\t    arm A  reproduces round 1's drive exactly — 0 steps, halted=true,\n17\t           the false negative in three lines\n18\t    arm B  adds the ONE missing line (tu/queue-rows!) and drives the same\n19\t           D2-compiled fixture through the same evaluator session: it\n20\t           completes under the 2M budget with the correct outcome —\n21\t           there is no non-terminating cycle in the evaluator session,\n22\t           the observer coordination, or any encoder layer\n23\t    arm C  shrinks the budget to 10000 steps and shows run-bounded's\n24\t           exhaustion throw PROPAGATES out of observer/run-on-stream\n25\t           (carry-session rethrows; it never feeds the loop), carrying\n26\t           the advanced machine under :consumer and the partial session\n27\t           under :session — the opt-in recovery data, not a retry cycle.\n28\t\n29\t  The kernel-c semantic path (`run-guest-machine`) has no encoder session\n30\t  in it at any commit: it is tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! +\n31\t  observer/run-on-stream, single stage. The two C lanes differ only in\n32\t  machine construction and loader.\"\n33\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n34\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n35\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n36\t            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n37\t            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n38\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n39\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n40\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n41\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n42\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n43\t\n44\t(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n45\t(def steps (atom 0))\n46\t\n47\t(defn- counted-step\n48\t  [machine]\n49\t  (swap! steps inc)\n50\t  (original-step machine))\n51\t\n52\t(defn- fixture-ast\n53\t  \"The D2-compiled check-assume-have-discharge fixture, as kernel-c sees it.\"\n54\t  []\n55\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n56\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n57\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)]\n58\t    (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n59\t      (throw (ex-info \"fixture no longer compiles\" {:status (:status compiled)})))\n60\t    (:ast compiled)))\n61\t\n62\t(defn- load-rows\n63\t  []\n64\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader\n65\t    (fn [m rows stamp]\n66\t      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n67\t      (semantic/load-vector m\n68\t                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n69\t                            vm/semantic-contract))\n70\t    vm/ast-contract))\n71\t\n72\t(defn- bounded-run\n73\t  \"run-guest-machine's runner, verbatim.\"\n74\t  [step-limit]\n75\t  (fn [machine]\n76\t    (loop [v machine n 0]\n77\t      (cond\n78\t        (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n79\t        (= n step-limit) (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n80\t                                         {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\n81\t        :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n))))))\n82\t\n83\t(defn- bounded [x]\n84\t  (let [s (pr-str x)]\n85\t    (if (> (count s) 200) (subs s 0 200) s)))\n86\t\n87\t(defn- arm-a-round-1-drive\n88\t  []\n89\t  (reset! steps 0)\n90\t  (let [machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n91\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n92\t                                     :modules (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)})\n93\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)] ;; medium is EMPTY\n94\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n95\t      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\n96\t                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\n97\t                                         (load-rows)\n98\t                                         (bounded-run 2000000))]\n99\t        {:steps @steps\n100\t         :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\n101\t         :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\n102\t         :queue-line :absent}))))\n103\t\n104\t(defn- arm-b-true-drive\n105\t  []\n106\t  (reset! steps 0)\n107\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n108\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n109\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n110\t                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\n111\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\n112\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n113\t      (let [done (as-> session s\n114\t                  (tu/queue-rows! s ast) ;; <- the ONE line round 1 omitted\n115\t                  (observer/run-on-stream s engine/ready-for-ingress?\n116\t                                          (load-rows) (bounded-run 2000000)))\n117\t            m (:consumer done)]\n118\t        {:steps @steps\n119\t         :halted (vm/halted? m)\n120\t         :blocked (vm/blocked? m)\n121\t         :outcome (bounded (vm/value m))}))))\n122\t\n123\t(defn- arm-c-exhaustion-propagates\n124\t  []\n125\t  (reset! steps 0)\n126\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n127\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n128\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n129\t                                     :modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)})\n130\t        session (tu/queue-rows! (tu/make-observer-session machine) ast)]\n131\t    (try\n132\t      (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step]\n133\t        (observer/run-on-stream session engine/ready-for-ingress?\n134\t                                (load-rows) (bounded-run 10000))\n135\t        {:propagated false})\n136\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n137\t        (let [d (ex-data e)\n138\t              consumer (:consumer d)]\n139\t          {:propagated true\n140\t           :message (ex-message e)\n141\t           :data-has-consumer (contains? d :consumer)\n142\t           :data-has-session (contains? d :session)\n143\t           :consumer-advanced {:halted (:halted? consumer)\n144\t                               :blocked (:blocked? consumer)\n145\t                               :cont-depth (count (:k consumer))\n146\t                               :control (select-keys (:control consumer) [:segment :pc])}\n147\t           :cause-preserved (some? (ex-cause e))})))))\n148\t\n149\t(defn- arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism\n150\t  \"What the gate does with the exhaustion throw: kernel-attempt's catch\n151\t  expands the exception data with `evidence-data` — dissoc'ing :session but\n152\t  NOT :consumer, which after a full 2M-step run is the entire advanced\n153\t  machine. This arm reproduces exactly that expansion in isolation, under a\n154\t  wall bound with a stack dump, so the gate's post-exhaustion freeze is\n155\t  attributable without running the corpus.\"\n156\t  []\n157\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n158\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\n159\t    (try\n160\t      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\n161\t      {:exhausted false}\n162\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n163\t        (let [data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session)  ;; kernel-attempt's own dissoc\n164\t              evidence (deref #'latte/evidence-data)\n165\t              t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n166\t              result (atom {:finished false})\n167\t              worker (doto (Thread. (fn []\n168\t                                      (try\n169\t                                        (let [v (evidence data)]\n170\t                                          (reset! result\n171\t                                                  {:finished true\n172\t                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n173\t                                                   :walked-keys (count v)}))\n174\t                                        (catch Throwable t\n175\t                                          (reset! result\n176\t                                                  {:finished true\n177\t                                                   :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n178\t                                                   :threw (ex-message t)})))))\n179\t                          (.setName \"arm-d-evidence-walk\")\n180\t                          (.setDaemon true))]\n181\t          (.start worker)\n182\t          (loop [waited 0]\n183\t            (Thread/sleep 5000)\n184\t            (let [r @result]\n185\t              (cond\n186\t                (:finished r) r\n187\t\n188\t                (>= waited 120000)\n189\t                (do (println :ARM-D-UNFINISHED-AFTER-MS waited)\n190\t                    (doseq [frame (take 25 (.getStackTrace worker))]\n191\t                      (println \"  \" (str frame)))\n192\t                    (flush)\n193\t                    {:finished false :capped-at-ms waited})\n194\t\n195\t                :else (recur (+ waited 5000))))))))))\n196\t\n197\t(defn- cycle-scan\n198\t  \"Identity-based DFS over the same shapes evidence-data/postwalk traverse\n199\t  (maps, vectors, seqs, sets, records). Reports unique node count, the\n200\t  deepest sharing, and — decisively — whether any container re-enters a node\n201\t  already on the DFS path: that is a true cycle, on which clojure.walk's\n202\t  postwalk (no seen-set) never terminates. Sharing off the path is normal\n203\t  persistent-structure DAG sharing and terminates.\"\n204\t  [x]\n205\t  (let [seen (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\n206\t        path (java.util.IdentityHashMap.)\n207\t        nodes (atom 0)\n208\t        shared (atom 0)\n209\t        cycle (atom nil)\n210\t        container? (fn [v] (or (map? v) (vector? v) (sequential? v) (set? v) (record? v)))\n211\t        children (fn [v]\n212\t                   (cond\n213\t                     (map? v) (concat (keys v) (vals v))\n214\t                     (record? v) (vals v)\n215\t                     :else (seq v)))]\n216\t    (letfn [(go [v depth]\n217\t              (when (> depth 200000) (throw (ex-info \"scan depth cap\" {:depth depth})))\n218\t              (when (container? v)\n219\t                (when (.containsKey path v)\n220\t                  (when-not @cycle (reset! cycle {:type (str (class v)) :at-depth depth}))\n221\t                  nil)\n222\t                (if (.containsKey seen v)\n223\t                  (do (swap! shared inc) nil)\n224\t                  (do (.put seen v true)\n225\t                      (.put path v true)\n226\t                      (swap! nodes inc)\n227\t                      (doseq [c (children v)] (go c (inc depth)))\n228\t                      (.remove path v)))))]\n229\t      (try\n230\t        (go x 0)\n231\t        (catch Throwable t {:scan-threw (ex-message t)}))\n232\t      {:unique-containers @nodes\n233\t       :shared-revisits @shared\n234\t       :cycle @cycle})))\n235\t\n236\t(defn- arm-e-cycle-scan\n237\t  \"Scan the exhausted machine itself (the :consumer from arm D's throw) for\n238\t  a cycle with the identity DFS above — the difference between an expensive\n239\t  finite expansion and a non-terminating one.\"\n240\t  []\n241\t  (let [ast (fixture-ast)\n242\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)]\n243\t    (try\n244\t      (compiler-test/run-guest-machine ast modules :walker 2000000)\n245\t      {:exhausted false}\n246\t      (catch clojure.lang.ExceptionInfo e\n247\t        (cycle-scan (:consumer (ex-data e)))))))\n248\t\n249\t(defn -main\n250\t  [& _args]\n251\t  (println :PIN {:commit \"8ea857c1+min-repro\" :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge})\n252\t  (println :ARM-A (arm-a-round-1-drive))\n253\t  (println :ARM-B (arm-b-true-drive))\n254\t  (println :ARM-C (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates))\n255\t  (println :ARM-D (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism))\n256\t  (println :ARM-E (arm-e-cycle-scan))\n257\t  (flush))\n258\t\n259\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-min-repro\n260\t  (testing \"diagnostic reproduction only — contributes zero coverage\"\n261\t    (let [a (arm-a-round-1-drive)\n262\t          _ (println :ARM-A a)\n263\t          b (arm-b-true-drive)\n264\t          _ (println :ARM-B b)\n265\t          c (arm-c-exhaustion-propagates)\n266\t          _ (println :ARM-C c)\n267\t          d (arm-d-gate-freeze-mechanism)\n268\t          _ (println :ARM-D d)\n269\t          e (arm-e-cycle-scan)\n270\t          _ (println :ARM-E e)]\n271\t      (is (zero? (:steps a)) \"arm A reproduces the round-1 false negative: no step ever ran\")\n272\t      (is (and (:halted a) (not (:blocked a)))\n273\t          \"arm A's machine reads halted only because create-vm mints :halted? true\")\n274\t      (is (and (:halted b) (pos? (:steps b)) (< (:steps b) 2000000))\n275\t          \"arm B: the same session with the fixture queued completes under the budget\")\n276\t      (is (and (:propagated c) (:data-has-consumer c) (:data-has-session c))\n277\t          \"arm C: the budget throw escapes run-on-stream carrying its recovery data\")\n278\t      (is (map? d) \"arm D reports the post-exhaustion evidence walk's cost shape\")\n279\t      (is (map? e) \"arm E reports the exhausted machine's cycle scan\")\n280\t      (flush))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_CuHwmKAboUjQ5MjypPZH73Bv","content":"1\t(ns d2-wedge-probe2\n2\t  \"H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2: drive the REAL kernel-c semantic path.\n3\t\n4\t  Round 1's probe (test/d2_wedge_probe.clj) never queued the fixture onto\n5\t  the session medium — `tu/make-observer-session` mints an EMPTY medium and\n6\t  the probe called no queue variant — so its evaluator-session drive was\n7\t  vacuous: a fresh SemanticVM is `:halted? true` (yin.vm.semantic/create-vm)\n8\t  before any step, and run-on-stream over an empty medium loads nothing and\n9\t  runs nothing. Stage A below reproduces that drive and measures its step\n10\t  count to confirm the false negative.\n11\t\n12\t  Stage B re-measures the exact kernel-c semantic path —\n13\t  `yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine`'s semantic branch\n14\t  (tu/make-observer-session + tu/queue-rows! + observer/run-on-stream +\n15\t  run-bounded over vm/step) — instrumented at vm/step (count, wall time,\n16\t  machine entering each step) and at the run-on-stream boundary (ready\n17\t  checks, batches loaded, run entries with per-run step deltas), with a\n18\t  watchdog that separates the three failure shapes:\n19\t\n20\t    - BUDGET-THROWN   run-bounded's 2M exhaustion throw reaches the caller\n21\t    - WEDGE-IN-STEP   step count frozen: one vm/step never returns; the\n22\t                      worker stack trace plus the entering machine are dumped\n23\t    - RATE-COLLAPSE   steps still advance but steps/sec decays toward zero;\n24\t                      the per-tick rate table plus a final snapshot are dumped\"\n25\t  (:require [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n26\t            [dao.stream.observer :as observer]\n27\t            [yang.clojure :as yang]\n28\t            [yang.clojure-test :as compiler-test]\n29\t            [yang.latte-oracle-test :as latte]\n30\t            [yin.vm :as vm]\n31\t            [yin.vm.engine :as engine]\n32\t            [yin.vm.semantic :as semantic]\n33\t            [yin.vm.semantic.linearize :as linearize]\n34\t            [yin.vm.test-utils :as tu]))\n35\t\n36\t(def ^:private original-step vm/step)\n37\t(def ^:private original-run-on-stream observer/run-on-stream)\n38\t\n39\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- instrumentation\n40\t\n41\t(def steps (atom 0))\n42\t(def in-step-nanos (atom 0))\n43\t(def recent-durations (atom []))          ;; last 64 step durations, nanos\n44\t(def last-machine (volatile! nil))        ;; machine entering the latest step\n45\t(def load-count (atom 0))\n46\t(def ready-count (atom 0))\n47\t(def run-log (atom []))                   ;; one entry per run-on-stream `run`\n48\t(def start-ms (atom nil))\n49\t\n50\t(defn- reset-instrumentation!\n51\t  []\n52\t  (reset! steps 0)\n53\t  (reset! in-step-nanos 0)\n54\t  (reset! recent-durations [])\n55\t  (vreset! last-machine nil)\n56\t  (reset! load-count 0)\n57\t  (reset! ready-count 0)\n58\t  (reset! run-log [])\n59\t  (reset! start-ms (System/currentTimeMillis)))\n60\t\n61\t(defn- counted-step\n62\t  [machine]\n63\t  (let [n (swap! steps inc)]\n64\t    (when (= n 1) (println :STEP-STARTED) (flush))\n65\t    (vreset! last-machine machine)\n66\t    (let [t0 (System/nanoTime)\n67\t          v (original-step machine)\n68\t          t1 (System/nanoTime)\n69\t          d (- t1 t0)]\n70\t      (swap! in-step-nanos + d)\n71\t      (swap! recent-durations (fn [r] (vec (take-last 64 (conj r d)))))\n72\t      v)))\n73\t\n74\t(defn- instrumented-run-on-stream\n75\t  [session ready? load run]\n76\t  (let [ready?* (fn [c] (swap! ready-count inc) (ready? c))\n77\t        load* (fn [c batch] (swap! load-count inc) (load c batch))\n78\t        run* (fn [c]\n79\t               (let [before @steps]\n80\t                 (try\n81\t                   (let [v (run c)]\n82\t                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\n83\t                                          :exit-steps @steps\n84\t                                          :threw false})\n85\t                     v)\n86\t                   (catch Throwable t\n87\t                     (swap! run-log conj {:entry-steps before\n88\t                                          :exit-steps @steps\n89\t                                          :threw (ex-message t)})\n90\t                     (throw t)))))]\n91\t    (original-run-on-stream session ready?* load* run*)))\n92\t\n93\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- state capture\n94\t\n95\t(defn- bounded-str\n96\t  [x]\n97\t  (let [s (pr-str x)]\n98\t    (if (> (count s) 240) (str (subs s 0 240) \"…\") s)))\n99\t\n100\t(defn- instruction-at\n101\t  \"The register instruction the machine's :control points at — op and\n102\t  operands, bounded. The instruction vector is static code, so its size is\n103\t  the compiler's, not the machine's.\"\n104\t  [machine]\n105\t  (try\n106\t    (let [{:keys [segment pc]} (:control machine)\n107\t          image (get (:code machine) segment)]\n108\t      (if (and image (number? pc) (vector? (:vector image)))\n109\t        (bounded-str (try (nth (:vector image) pc)\n110\t                          (catch Exception e\n111\t                            {:nth-failed (ex-message e)})))\n112\t        {:segment segment :pc pc :image (nil? image)}))\n113\t    (catch Exception e {:unreadable (ex-message e)})))\n114\t\n115\t(defn- machine-snapshot\n116\t  \"Bounded view of one machine: no closures, no environments, no stores.\"\n117\t  [m]\n118\t  (when m\n119\t    (let [k (:k m)\n120\t          top (when (vector? k) (peek k))]\n121\t      {:halted? (:halted? m)\n122\t       :blocked? (:blocked? m)\n123\t       :cont-depth (if (vector? k) (count k) (when k 1))\n124\t       :control (when-let [c (:control m)] (select-keys c [:segment :pc]))\n125\t       :control-inst (instruction-at m)\n126\t       :top-frame (when (map? top) (select-keys top [:type :segment :pc :rd]))\n127\t       :wait-set (count (or (:wait-set m) []))\n128\t       :ready-queue (count (or (:ready-queue m) []))\n129\t       :window-size (count (:window m))\n130\t       :value (bounded-str (:value m))})))\n131\t\n132\t(defn- duration-stats\n133\t  []\n134\t  (let [rs @recent-durations]\n135\t    (when (seq rs)\n136\t      (let [sorted (sort rs)]\n137\t        {:n (count sorted)\n138\t         :min-ns (first sorted)\n139\t         :p50-ns (nth sorted (quot (count sorted) 2))\n140\t         :max-ns (last sorted)}))))\n141\t\n142\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage A\n143\t\n144\t(defn- make-load-rows\n145\t  []\n146\t  (vm/fresh-code-loader\n147\t    (fn [m rows stamp]\n148\t      (vm/check-contract! vm/ast-contract stamp)\n149\t      (semantic/load-vector m\n150\t                            (:vector (linearize/project-rows rows))\n151\t                            vm/semantic-contract))\n152\t    vm/ast-contract))\n153\t\n154\t(defn- old-probe-bounded-run\n155\t  \"Round 1's runner, verbatim semantics.\"\n156\t  [machine]\n157\t  (loop [v machine n 0]\n158\t    (cond\n159\t      (or (vm/halted? v) (vm/blocked? v)) v\n160\t      (= n 2000000)\n161\t      (throw (ex-info \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"\n162\t                      {:lane :semantic :steps n :consumer v}))\n163\t      :else (recur (vm/step v) (inc n)))))\n164\t\n165\t(defn- stage-a-vacuity\n166\t  \"Reproduce round 1's evaluator-session drive exactly — including its\n167\t  missing queue step — and measure how many steps it actually executed.\"\n168\t  []\n169\t  (println :STAGE-A :round-1-probe-reproduction\n170\t           {:medium :empty-at-start :queue :absent-as-in-round-1})\n171\t  (flush)\n172\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\n173\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n174\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n175\t        ;; round 1 compiled the fixture and never used the result; the call\n176\t        ;; itself is kept so stage A matches that run's cost shape\n177\t        _ ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n178\t        lm (deref #'compiler-test/library-modules)\n179\t        machine (semantic/create-vm {:make-stream tu/make-stream\n180\t                                     :capability-secret tu/secret\n181\t                                     :modules lm})\n182\t        session (tu/make-observer-session machine)]\n183\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n184\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n185\t      (let [done (observer/run-on-stream session\n186\t                                         engine/ready-for-ingress?\n187\t                                         (make-load-rows)\n188\t                                         old-probe-bounded-run)]\n189\t        (println :STAGE-A-RESULT\n190\t                 {:steps @steps\n191\t                  :loads @load-count\n192\t                  :halted (vm/halted? (:consumer done))\n193\t                  :blocked (vm/blocked? (:consumer done))\n194\t                  :verdict (if (zero? @steps)\n195\t                             :VACUOUS-no-program-ever-loaded\n196\t                             :REAL-round1-was-valid)})\n197\t        (flush)))))\n198\t\n199\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage B\n200\t\n201\t(def ^:private tick-ms 10000)\n202\t(def ^:private wall-cap-ms 1800000)\n203\t(def ^:private frozen-ticks 3)\n204\t\n205\t(defn- print-tick\n206\t  [t steps-prev]\n207\t  (let [n @steps\n208\t        in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n209\t        elapsed (quot (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) 1000)\n210\t        m @last-machine\n211\t        k (:k m)\n212\t        stats (duration-stats)\n213\t        rate (if (>= steps-prev 0)\n214\t               (quot (* (- n steps-prev) 1000) t)\n215\t               :first-tick)]\n216\t    (println :TICK {:s elapsed :steps n :in-step-ms in-step-ms\n217\t                    :steps-per-s-last-tick rate\n218\t                    :step-ns stats\n219\t                    :cont-depth (when (vector? k) (count k))\n220\t                    :loads @load-count :runs (count @run-log)})\n221\t    (flush)\n222\t    n))\n223\t\n224\t(defn- dump-state\n225\t  [worker label]\n226\t  (println label {:steps @steps\n227\t                  :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n228\t                  :loads @load-count\n229\t                  :ready-checks @ready-count\n230\t                  :runs @run-log\n231\t                  :entering-machine (machine-snapshot @last-machine)})\n232\t  (when worker\n233\t    (println :WORKER-STACK)\n234\t    (doseq [frame (take 60 (.getStackTrace worker))]\n235\t      (println \"  \" (str frame)))\n236\t    (flush)))\n237\t\n238\t(defn- stage-b-real-path\n239\t  []\n240\t  (println :STAGE-B :real-kernel-c-semantic-path\n241\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n242\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n243\t            :step-limit 2000000\n244\t            :wall-cap-ms wall-cap-ms})\n245\t  (flush)\n246\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\n247\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n248\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n249\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n250\t        _ (when-not (= :compiled (:status compiled))\n251\t            (println :STAGE-B-BLOCKED-AT-COMPILE\n252\t                     (select-keys compiled [:status :blocked-by]))\n253\t            (flush))\n254\t        ast (:ast compiled)\n255\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n256\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\n257\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\n258\t                          (try\n259\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n260\t                                            ast modules :semantic 2000000)]\n261\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n262\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\n263\t                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\n264\t                            (catch Throwable t\n265\t                              (reset! result\n266\t                                      {:kind :threw\n267\t                                       :class (str (class t))\n268\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\n269\t                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\n270\t                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\n271\t                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\n272\t                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\n273\t                                                           (:consumer\n274\t                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\n275\t    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n276\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\n277\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n278\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n279\t      (.start worker)\n280\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n281\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n282\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n283\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n284\t          (cond\n285\t            (not alive)\n286\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n287\t                                             :steps @steps\n288\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n289\t                                             :loads @load-count\n290\t                                             :ready-checks @ready-count\n291\t                                             :runs @run-log))\n292\t                (flush)\n293\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\n294\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n295\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n296\t                  (System/exit 4)))\n297\t\n298\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n299\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n300\t\n301\t            (and n (= n prev))\n302\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n303\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n304\t                  (System/exit 3))\n305\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n306\t\n307\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n308\t\n309\t(defn -main\n310\t  [& _args]\n311\t  (println :PIN {:commit \"8ea857c1+probe2\"\n312\t                 :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n313\t                 :lane :semantic\n314\t                 :budget \"2M instrumented steps\"\n315\t                 :jvm (str (System/getProperty \"java.version\"))})\n316\t  (flush)\n317\t  (stage-a-vacuity)\n318\t  (stage-b-real-path))\n319\t\n320\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2\n321\t  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n322\t    (-main)\n323\t    (is true)))\n324\t\n325\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage C\n326\t\n327\t;; Stage B showed the fixture's own semantic cell completes (1.1M steps,\n328\t;; seconds of stepping) when driven alone. The reported stalls were observed\n329\t;; on the whole-corpus gate, so stage C drives the gate itself — every\n330\t;; fixture's A/B/compile/walker/semantic legs — under timing wrappers and\n331\t;; the vm/step counter, with freeze detection that dumps the worker stack\n332\t;; wherever the run stops advancing (C lane stepping, host A/B eval, or\n333\t;; anywhere else).\n334\t\n335\t(def ^:private gate-frozen-ticks 30)          ;; 5 min without a step\n336\t(def ^:private gate-wall-cap-ms 5400000)      ;; the longest observed trial\n337\t\n338\t(defn- wall-ms-since\n339\t  [t0]\n340\t  (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0))\n341\t\n342\t(defn- stage-c-gate\n343\t  []\n344\t  (println :STAGE-C :full-differential-gate\n345\t           {:test 'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate\n346\t            :freeze-ticks gate-frozen-ticks\n347\t            :wall-cap-ms gate-wall-cap-ms})\n348\t  (flush)\n349\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\n350\t  (let [gate-t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n351\t        leg (fn [label f]\n352\t              (fn [& args]\n353\t                (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n354\t                      before @steps\n355\t                      r (apply f args)]\n356\t                  (println :LEG label\n357\t                           {:wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n358\t                            :steps (- @steps before)\n359\t                            :arg0 (bounded-str (first args))})\n360\t                  (flush)\n361\t                  r)))\n362\t        orig-kernel-a (deref #'latte/kernel-a)\n363\t        orig-kernel-b (deref #'latte/kernel-b)\n364\t        orig-kernel-compile (deref #'latte/kernel-compile)\n365\t        orig-kernel-c (deref #'latte/kernel-c)\n366\t        orig-kernel-row (deref #'latte/kernel-row)\n367\t        kernel-c* (fn [compiled lane]\n368\t                    (let [before @steps]\n369\t                      (println :C-ENTER {:lane lane\n370\t                                         :at-steps before\n371\t                                         :total-s (quot (wall-ms-since gate-t0) 1000)})\n372\t                      (flush)\n373\t                      (let [t0 (System/currentTimeMillis)\n374\t                            r (orig-kernel-c compiled lane)]\n375\t                        (println :C-EXIT {:lane lane\n376\t                                          :wall-ms (- (System/currentTimeMillis) t0)\n377\t                                          :steps (- @steps before)\n378\t                                          :status (:status r)\n379\t                                          :outcome-tag (-> r :outcome first)})\n380\t                        (flush)\n381\t                        r)))\n382\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\n383\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\n384\t                          (try\n385\t                            ;; test-var output goes to this process's stdout\n386\t                            ;; on purpose: the gate's own KERNEL-FIXTURE lines\n387\t                            ;; are the live mid-fixture progress signal.\n388\t                            (clojure.test/test-var\n389\t                              #'yang.latte-oracle-test/test-kernel-differential-gate)\n390\t                            (reset! result {:kind :returned\n391\t                                            :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})\n392\t                            (catch Throwable t\n393\t                              (reset! result {:kind :threw\n394\t                                              :class (str (class t))\n395\t                                              :message (ex-message t)\n396\t                                              :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)})))))]\n397\t    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n398\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\n399\t    (with-redefs-fn {#'vm/step counted-step\n400\t                     #'observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream\n401\t                     #'latte/kernel-a (leg :a orig-kernel-a)\n402\t                     #'latte/kernel-b (leg :b orig-kernel-b)\n403\t                     #'latte/kernel-compile (leg :compile orig-kernel-compile)\n404\t                     #'latte/kernel-c kernel-c*\n405\t                     #'latte/kernel-row (leg :row orig-kernel-row)}\n406\t      (fn []\n407\t        (.start worker)\n408\t        (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n409\t          (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n410\t          (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n411\t                n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n412\t            (cond\n413\t              (not alive)\n414\t              (do (println :GATE-DONE (assoc @result\n415\t                                             :steps @steps\n416\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n417\t                                             :wall-ms (wall-ms-since gate-t0)\n418\t                                             :runs @run-log))\n419\t                  (flush)\n420\t                  (condp = (:kind @result)\n421\t                    :returned (System/exit 0)\n422\t                    :threw (System/exit 1)\n423\t                    (System/exit 4)))\n424\t\n425\t              (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) gate-t0) (long gate-wall-cap-ms))\n426\t              (do (dump-state worker :GATE-WALL-CAP-REACHED) (System/exit 2))\n427\t\n428\t              (and n (= n prev))\n429\t              (do (when (>= (inc frozen) gate-frozen-ticks)\n430\t                    (dump-state worker :GATE-FROZEN-5MIN)\n431\t                    (System/exit 3))\n432\t                  (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n433\t\n434\t              :else (recur (or n prev) 0))))))))\n435\t\n436\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-gate\n437\t  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n438\t    (stage-c-gate)\n439\t    (is true)))\n440\t\n441\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage D\n442\t\n443\t;; The in-gate freeze sat in check-assume-have-discharge's WALKER cell: it\n444\t;; consumed exactly its whole 2,000,000-step budget and then the run never\n445\t;; returned while no step advanced. Stage D drives that one cell in\n446\t;; isolation — same driver, same instrumentation — to (a) confirm the\n447\t;; exhaustion reproduces without the corpus context and (b) capture the\n448\t;; bounded exhaustion state: the advanced :consumer's halted/blocked flags,\n449\t;; continuation depth, control, and the top frame.\n450\t\n451\t(defn- stage-d-walker\n452\t  []\n453\t  (println :STAGE-D :walker-cell-in-isolation\n454\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n455\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n456\t            :step-limit 2000000})\n457\t  (flush)\n458\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\n459\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n460\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n461\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n462\t        ast (:ast compiled)\n463\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n464\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\n465\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\n466\t                          (try\n467\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n468\t                                            ast modules :walker 2000000)]\n469\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n470\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)}))\n471\t                            (catch Throwable t\n472\t                              (reset! result\n473\t                                      {:kind :threw\n474\t                                       :class (str (class t))\n475\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\n476\t                                       :data-keys (vec (keys (ex-data t)))\n477\t                                       :consumer (machine-snapshot\n478\t                                                   (:consumer (ex-data t)))\n479\t                                       :session-consumer (machine-snapshot\n480\t                                                           (:consumer\n481\t                                                             (:session (ex-data t))))})))))]\n482\t    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n483\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\n484\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n485\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n486\t      (.start worker)\n487\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n488\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n489\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n490\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n491\t          (cond\n492\t            (not alive)\n493\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n494\t                                             :steps @steps\n495\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n496\t                                             :loads @load-count\n497\t                                             :runs @run-log))\n498\t                (flush)\n499\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\n500\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n501\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n502\t                  (System/exit 4)))\n503\t\n504\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n505\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n506\t\n507\t            (and n (= n prev))\n508\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n509\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n510\t                  (System/exit 3))\n511\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n512\t\n513\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n514\t\n515\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker\n516\t  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n517\t    (stage-d-walker)\n518\t    (is true)))\n519\t\n520\t;; ---------------------------------------------------------------- stage F\n521\t\n522\t;; The walker cell now exhausts 2M (stage D) while the semantic cell\n523\t;; completes at 1.1M (stage B). How far over the budget is the walker?\n524\t;; One bounded diagnostic trial at 8M — the H3-1 round's authorized trial\n525\t;; ladder — reporting the walker's true completion count, or a second\n526\t;; exhaustion. Diagnostic configuration only: NOT an acceptance-budget\n527\t;; proposal.\n528\t\n529\t(defn- stage-f-walker-8m\n530\t  []\n531\t  (println :STAGE-F :walker-cell-8m-trial\n532\t           {:driver 'yang.clojure-test/run-guest-machine\n533\t            :fixture :check-assume-have-discharge\n534\t            :step-limit 8000000})\n535\t  (flush)\n536\t  (reset-instrumentation!)\n537\t  (let [fixture (first (filter #(= :check-assume-have-discharge (:id %))\n538\t                               (:fixtures (deref #'latte/kernel-gate-corpus))))\n539\t        compiled ((deref #'latte/kernel-compile) fixture)\n540\t        ast (:ast compiled)\n541\t        modules ((deref #'latte/oracle-registry) yang/kind-module)\n542\t        result (atom {:kind :none})\n543\t        worker (Thread. (fn []\n544\t                          (try\n545\t                            (let [machine (compiler-test/run-guest-machine\n546\t                                            ast modules :walker 8000000)]\n547\t                              (reset! result {:kind :returned\n548\t                                              :steps @steps\n549\t                                              :machine (machine-snapshot machine)\n550\t                                              :value (bounded-str (vm/value machine))}))\n551\t                            (catch Throwable t\n552\t                              (reset! result\n553\t                                      {:kind :threw\n554\t                                       :class (str (class t))\n555\t                                       :message (ex-message t)\n556\t                                       :steps @steps})))))]\n557\t    (.setName worker \"wedge-worker\")\n558\t    (.setDaemon worker true)\n559\t    (with-redefs [vm/step counted-step\n560\t                  observer/run-on-stream instrumented-run-on-stream]\n561\t      (.start worker)\n562\t      (loop [prev -1 frozen 0]\n563\t        (Thread/sleep (long tick-ms))\n564\t        (let [alive (.isAlive worker)\n565\t              n (when alive (print-tick tick-ms prev))]\n566\t          (cond\n567\t            (not alive)\n568\t            (do (println :WORKER-DONE (assoc @result\n569\t                                             :in-step-ms (quot @in-step-nanos 1000000)\n570\t                                             :loads @load-count\n571\t                                             :runs @run-log))\n572\t                (flush)\n573\t                (condp = (:kind @result)\n574\t                  :returned (System/exit 0)\n575\t                  :threw (System/exit 1)\n576\t                  (System/exit 4)))\n577\t\n578\t            (>= (- (System/currentTimeMillis) @start-ms) (long wall-cap-ms))\n579\t            (do (dump-state worker :RATE-COLLAPSE-WALL-CAP) (System/exit 2))\n580\t\n581\t            (and n (= n prev))\n582\t            (do (when (>= (inc frozen) frozen-ticks)\n583\t                  (dump-state worker :WEDGE-CONFIRMED-IN-STEP)\n584\t                  (System/exit 3))\n585\t                (recur (or n prev) (inc frozen)))\n586\t\n587\t            :else (recur (or n prev) 0)))))))\n588\t\n589\t(deftest test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker-8m\n590\t  (testing \"diagnostic probe only — contributes zero coverage\"\n591\t    (stage-f-walker-8m)\n592\t    (is true)))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_cjbnlf9Hm5RDggcFuke6YRJF","content":"1\t# H3-1 wedge diagnostic, round 2 — the findings report\n2\t\n3\tCreated: 2026-11-04 (GMT) · Agent: glm (glm-5.3) · Branch: `hardening3-h3-1` at `8ea857c1`\n4\tTask: BRIEF-wedge.md (per the architect's continuation ruling, steps 3–4)\n5\tArtifacts: `test/d2_wedge_probe2.clj` (stages A–D, F + gate stage C),\n6\t`test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj` (arms A–E); evidence logs in this directory\n7\t(`1794100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-run1|-gate1|-walker1|-walker8m|.minrepro.log`)\n8\t\n9\t## Verdict in one paragraph\n10\t\n11\tThere is **no non-terminating loop in the encoder session layer, the observer\n12\tcoordination, or the semantic evaluator** — and the kernel-c semantic path\n13\tcontains no encoder session at any commit. The round-1 \"evaluator terminates /\n14\twedge lives in the encoder session layer\" split was an artifact of a vacuous\n15\tprobe. The gate stall that motivated this round is real, it reproduces, and it\n16\tlives **after** the walker cell's legitimate budget exhaustion: the gate's\n17\t`kernel-attempt` hands the exhaustion exception's `:consumer` — the entire\n18\tadvanced machine — to `evidence-data` → `upstream-record-data`, whose\n19\t`clojure.walk/postwalk` re-expands it with five `requiring-resolve` calls per\n20\tnode and no cycle guard. That host-side walk, not any VM loop, is what burns\n21\t2400s+ with zero guest steps. D2's real regression is smaller and factual: it\n22\tpushed this fixture's **walker** cell over the 2M budget (the semantic cell\n23\tstill completes at 1.1M).\n24\t\n25\t## 1. Round 1's probe was vacuous — the layer-location built on it is retracted\n26\t\n27\t`test/d2_wedge_probe.clj` builds `semantic/create-vm` + `tu/make-observer-session`\n28\tand calls `observer/run-on-stream` — but **never queues the fixture onto the\n29\tmedium** (no `tu/queue-rows!` anywhere in the file). An observer session over\n30\tan empty medium observes nothing (`:retry`/`:ended`), never calls `load`, never\n31\tenters `run`. And a fresh `SemanticVM` is minted `:halted? true`\n32\t(`src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:432`), so the untouched machine reads \"halted\".\n33\t\n34\tMeasured (stage A, `…-probe2-run1.log` in this directory):\n35\t\n36\t```\n37\t:STAGE-A-RESULT {:steps 0, :loads 0, :halted true, :blocked false,\n38\t                 :verdict :VACUOUS-no-program-ever-loaded}\n39\t```\n40\t\n41\tZero steps. The \"terminates, halted, well under 2M\" measurement in commit\n42\t`8ea857c1` measured a machine that never executed an instruction.\n43\t\n44\tThe same commit message's premise — \"kernel-c wraps the machine in\n45\ttu/make-encoder-session + encoder/forward-on-stream\" — is false at `8ea857c1`\n46\tand at every commit since `run-guest-machine` was introduced (`7723c6ae`): the\n47\tkernel-c path is `tu/make-observer-session` + `tu/queue-rows!`/`queue-ast!` +\n48\tone `observer/run-on-stream` call (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1995-2009`),\n49\tsingle stage, no encoder. The only encoder references in `clojure_test.clj`\n50\tare the descriptor tests (lines 785, 1028, 1047).\n51\t\n52\t## 2. The real kernel-c semantic cell completes (stage B)\n53\t\n54\tDriving the exact kernel-c semantic call —\n55\t`run-guest-machine ast (oracle-registry yang/kind-module) :semantic 2000000` —\n56\tinstrumented at `vm/step` and at the `run-on-stream` boundary:\n57\t\n58\t```\n59\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :returned,\n60\t              :steps 1105792, :in-step-ms 2535, :loads 1, :ready-checks 3,\n61\t              :runs [{:entry-steps 0, :exit-steps 1105792, :threw false}],\n62\t              :halted true, :blocked false,\n63\t              :value [:yin.k/ok [:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] (Π [B ✳] …))]]]}\n64\t```\n65\t\n66\t1,105,792 steps (55% of budget), 2.5 s of stepping, correct proof outcome. This\n67\tmatches the pre-D2 measurement (`0dc54289`: both fixtures complete inside 2M\n68\tafter the call-lowering fix) — D2 did not make the semantic cell explode.\n69\t\n70\t## 3. The observer/encoder layer cannot be the loop (code + measurement)\n71\t\n72\tThe brief's candidate — the budget throw caught by `carry-session` and fed back\n73\tvia `consumer-left-by-run` — does not exist:\n74\t\n75\t- `carry-session` (`src/cljc/dao/stream/observer.cljc:211-214`) **rethrows**:\n76\t  `(throw (ex-info … (assoc (ex-data e) :session session) e))`. Both catch\n77\t  sites in `run-on-stream` (`observer.cljc:250-255` and `277-282`) call it\n78\t  directly; neither recurs.\n79\t- `consumer-left-by-run` (`observer.cljc:183-196`) only reads `:consumer` from\n80\t  the exception's data to attach to the carried `:session`. It is never a loop\n81\t  variable; no caller re-enters `run` with it inside this harness.\n82\t- `run-on-stream`'s loop re-enters only on `:advance` (a batch observed), `:gap`\n83\t  (recovery cursor), or not-ready→run→ready. This harness queues exactly one\n84\t  batch: measured `loads 1, runs 1`.\n85\t- Arm C of the minimized reproduction drives the semantic cell at a 10,000-step\n86\t  budget: the exhaustion throw **propagates out** of `run-on-stream` with\n87\t  `:consumer` (advanced machine), `:session` (partial session), and the cause\n88\t  preserved. Recovery is opt-in data for callers; there is no retry cycle.\n89\t\n90\t## 4. Where the gate actually stalls — the exact site, caught in the act\n91\t\n92\tStage C drove the full 106-fixture differential gate\n93\t(`test-kernel-differential-gate`) under the same instrumentation with a\n94\tfreeze detector. It froze mid-corpus, in `check-assume-have-discharge`\n95\t(fixture 50 of 106), **inside the walker C cell** — the opposite lane from the\n96\tD2 report's attribution:\n97\t\n98\t```\n99\t:LEG :a …wall-ms 5      (check-assume-have-discharge)\n100\t:LEG :b …wall-ms 89\n101\t:LEG :compile …wall-ms 51\n102\t:C-ENTER {:lane :walker, :at-steps 3786531, :total-s 91}\n103\t   … steps advance to 5786531 (= 3786531 + exactly 2000000) in ~20 s …\n104\t   … then zero steps for ≥300 s; no :C-EXIT ever prints; detector fired\n105\t```\n106\t\n107\tThe captured worker stack (top frames, full dump in\n108\t`1794100000000-engineer-h3-1-wedge.probe2-gate1.log` in this directory):\n109\t\n110\t```\n111\tclojure.lang.Var.getThreadBinding → requiring-resolve\n112\tyang.latte_oracle_test$upstream_fn.invokeStatic        (latte_oracle_test.clj:286)\n113\tyang.latte_oracle_test$upstream_record_data$…invoke    (latte_oracle_test.clj:1025)\n114\tclojure.walk$postwalk → into → reduce → LazySeq.force → clojure.walk$postwalk …\n115\t```\n116\t\n117\tThe causal chain, with line references:\n118\t\n119\t1. `run-bounded` (`test/yang/clojure_test.clj:1987-1993`) counts 2,000,000\n120\t   walker steps — the walker cell of this fixture now **exhausts** the budget\n121\t   (it completed inside 2M before D2) — and throws\n122\t   `\"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"` with `{:lane … :steps … :consumer v}`\n123\t   (`clojure_test.clj:1991-1992`; the `:consumer` addition is the H3-1 fix\n124\t   round's own one-line harness change).\n125\t2. `run-on-stream`'s run-catch (`observer.cljc:277-282`) wraps via\n126\t   `carry-session` — a cheap rethrow adding `:session`.\n127\t3. `kernel-c`'s body runs inside `kernel-attempt`\n128\t   (`test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1659-1671`), whose catch builds\n129\t   `:data (evidence-data (dissoc (ex-data e) :session))` — it strips `:session`\n130\t   but **not `:consumer`**, so the entire advanced machine enters\n131\t   `evidence-data`.\n132\t4. `evidence-data` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1645-1656`) hits `(record? x)` — the\n133\t   machine is a record — and calls `upstream-record-data`\n134\t   (`latte_oracle_test.clj:1014-1028`): a `clojure.walk/postwalk` over the\n135\t   whole machine that calls `(upstream-fn pred)` — i.e.\n136\t   `requiring-resolve` (`latte_oracle_test.clj:284-286`) — **five times per\n137\t   node**, then `evidence-data` recurses into every child, and every child\n138\t   record (each VM `Closure`/`Continuation` is a record) triggers another full\n139\t   `postwalk` of its subtree.\n140\t\n141\tThat is the \"wedge\": an unbounded, zero-guest-step, host-side expansion of the\n142\texhausted machine. Whether it is truly non-terminating (a cyclic closure\n143\tenvironment — recursive guest functions whose captured env binds their own\n144\tclosure record, on which `postwalk`, which has no seen-set, never terminates)\n145\tor merely hours-scale (per-record re-walk of shared env chains × five\n146\t`requiring-resolve` per node) is settled by the cycle scan in §6.\n147\t\n148\tThis also re-explains the D2-era observations without the encoder theory: the\n149\t2400 s/5400 s \"semantic cell wall-clock explosion\" runs were this same\n150\tpost-exhaustion expansion, mid-corpus, with no per-cell attribution recorded\n151\t(\"guest-step counts NOT yet captured\" in `805d81d6`'s message).\n152\t\n153\t## 5. The exhausted walker cell in isolation (stage D) — bounded state capture\n154\t\n155\tSame driver, walker lane, alone (no corpus context):\n156\t\n157\t```\n158\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :threw, :message \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\",\n159\t              :steps 2000000, :in-step-ms 10591, :loads 1,\n160\t              :runs [{:entry-steps 0, :exit-steps 2000000,\n161\t                      :threw \"Guest instruction budget exhausted\"}],\n162\t              :data-keys [:lane :steps :consumer :session],\n163\t              :consumer {:halted? false, :blocked? false, :cont-depth 1,\n164\t                         :control {}, :wait-set 0, :ready-queue 0,\n165\t                         :value [\"_\" 6]}}\n166\t```\n167\t\n168\tThe exhaustion itself is fast (≈11 s) and well-behaved: the throw propagates,\n169\t`:consumer`/`:session` ride along exactly as the recovery design intends. The\n170\tbrief's requested capture at wedge time: the advanced consumer is **neither\n171\thalted nor blocked**, continuation depth 1, mid-walk control, gensym value\n172\t`[\"_\" 6]` — the walker died inside fresh-supply generation under the proof\n173\tloop, not in any stream or admission machinery.\n174\t\n175\t## 6. Minimized reproduction — `test/d2_wedge_min_repro.clj`\n176\t\n177\tFive arms, each runnable alone (`clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-min-repro -v\n178\td2-wedge-min-repro/test-h31-wedge-min-repro`, ≈4–6 min):\n179\t\n180\t- **arm A** — round 1's drive, verbatim (session, no queue):\n181\t  `{0 steps, halted true}` — the false negative in three lines.\n182\t- **arm B** — the same session plus the one omitted line (`tu/queue-rows!`):\n183\t  completes at **1,105,792 steps**, halted, correct outcome.\n184\t- **arm C** — semantic at a 10,000-step budget: the throw escapes\n185\t  `run-on-stream` carrying `:consumer` + `:session`; recovery is opt-in.\n186\t- **arm D** — the gate freeze mechanism, isolated: drive the walker cell to its\n187\t  exhaustion throw, then time exactly kernel-attempt's\n188\t  `(evidence-data (dissoc ex-data :session))` under a 120 s cap with a stack\n189\t  dump. Result: **unfinished after the 120 s cap** — stack shows the same\n190\t  `clojure.walk$postwalk` recursion the gate freeze showed. The walker drive\n191\t  itself took ≈11 s; the post-throw expansion is >10× that and still running\n192\t  when capped.\n193\t- **arm E** — an identity-based DFS cycle scan over the exhausted `:consumer`\n194\t  (the same shapes `evidence-data`/`postwalk` traverse), reporting unique\n195\t  container count, off-path sharing, and whether any node re-enters the DFS\n196\t  path (a true cycle ⇒ `postwalk` never terminates). Result:\n197\t  `{:unique-containers 78913, :shared-revisits 3442, :cycle nil}` — **no\n198\t  cycle**. The machine is a finite DAG, so the walk terminates *eventually*;\n199\t  its cost is the re-expansion: every record child (each VM Closure/\n200\t  Continuation) triggers `upstream-record-data`'s own full postwalk of its\n201\t  subtree, and the 3,442 sharing points make those subtrees overlap —\n202\t  finite-but-astronomical, which is exactly the shape \"2400 s × 2 stalled,\n203\t  5400 s never returned\" describes: not an infinite loop, an expansion that\n204\t  had not finished inside the trial window.\n205\t\n206\t## 7. How far over the budget is the walker? (stage F — bounded trial)\n207\t\n208\tAt an 8,000,000-step budget the walker cell **completes at 2,024,912 steps**\n209\t(11.8 s in-step) with the same correct outcome as the semantic cell:\n210\t\n211\t```\n212\t:WORKER-DONE {:kind :returned, :steps 2024912, :halted true,\n213\t              :value [:yin.k/ok [:ok [(<a>) (Π [A ✳] …)]]]}\n214\t```\n215\t\n216\tThe walker misses the 2M budget by **24,912 steps — 1.2%**. D2's per-call\n217\tpacket dispatch pushed a cell that previously completed inside 2M (commit\n218\t`0dc54289`) just barely over, and the harness's post-exhaustion expansion\n219\tturned that near-miss into the multi-hour \"wedge\". The semantic cell needs\n220\t1,105,792 (55% of budget).\n221\t\n222\t## 8. Recommendation\n223\t\n224\t1. **No yin.vm / observer / encoder architectural ruling is needed.** Nothing\n225\t   in `src/cljc/**` non-terminates or misbehaves; the observer recovery\n226\t   protocol did exactly what it is designed to do. No shared-runtime change is\n227\t   requested.\n228\t2. **The gate stall is a one-line harness defect** in\n229\t   `test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj:1667`: `kernel-attempt`'s catch feeds the\n230\t   exhaustion's `:consumer` machine to `evidence-data`. The comment above that\n231\t   very line already classifies `:session` as \"diagnostic machinery, not a\n232\t   portable domain payload; recursively expanding its closure environments\n233\t   duplicates the whole program\" — `:consumer` is the same class of payload.\n234\t   Proposed next-round fix: `(dissoc (ex-data e) :session :consumer)`, or\n235\t   replace `:consumer` with a bounded snapshot (halted/blocked/cont-depth/\n236\t   control) before expansion. latte_oracle_test.clj is out of bounds THIS\n237\t   round by the brief, so this is a recommendation, not a change.\n238\t3. **The D2 landing decision should be re-based on these numbers:** semantic\n239\t   cell 1,105,792 steps (completes); walker cell >2,000,000 (exhausts; see §7\n240\t   for the true count). The \"wall-clock explosion\" was the harness amplifying\n241\t   the walker's exhaustion, but the exhaustion itself is D2's per-call packet\n242\t   dispatch cost on the walker lane. Whatever the landing round decides\n243\t   (budget raise is DEFERRED by ruling; trimming the dispatch is a compiler\n244\t   change requiring its own scope), it no longer needs to explain a semantic\n245\t   wedge.\n246\t4. **Correct the record:** commit `8ea857c1`'s conclusion line (\"the wedge\n247\t   lives in the encoder session layer\") should be superseded by this report;\n248\t   `test/d2_wedge_probe.clj` should either gain its missing queue line or be\n249\t   retired in favor of `d2_wedge_probe2.clj` (this round leaves it untouched —\n250\t   it is the previous round's committed artifact and the kimi gate reviews\n251\t   before landing).\n252\t\n253\t## Reproduction ladder (all at `8ea857c1`, JVM 17, -Xss64m, this worktree)\n254\t\n255\t| run | command | outcome |\n256\t|-----|---------|---------|\n257\t| stage A+B | `clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-probe2 -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2` | A vacuous (0 steps); B returns at 1,105,792 steps |\n258\t| stage C (gate) | `clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-probe2 -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-gate` | frozen mid-corpus in the walker cell of check-assume-have-discharge; stack = evidence-data/postwalk; exit 3 by design |\n259\t| stage D (walker isolated) | `… -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker` | throws at exactly 2,000,000 steps in ≈11 s |\n260\t| stage F (8M trial) | `… -v d2-wedge-probe2/test-h31-wedge-probe2-walker-8m` | returns at 2,024,912 steps (1.2% over the 2M budget) |\n261\t| min-repro A–E | `clojure -M:test -n d2-wedge-min-repro -v d2-wedge-min-repro/test-h31-wedge-min-repro` | A 0 steps; B 1,105,792; C throw propagates; D >120 s unfinished (stack = postwalk); E 78,913 containers, 3,442 shared, no cycle |\n262\t\n263\tclj-kondo on both new files: 0 errors, 0 warnings (run through the lane's\n264\tProcessBuilder shim, deleted after)."}
