arities; these diagnostic probes add no arity coverage.\n5. Complete the independently validated nonvacuous authenticity regression before landing; earlier reported forgery tests are not sufficient evidence by assertion alone.\n\n### 3. Bar for any future intra-unit proposal\n\nAny replacement or revision must preserve:\n\n- Strictly unary published entry.\n- Compiler-held token authentication; no guest-reachable private lane or body application on refusal.\n- Dynamic admission and existing refusal behavior.\n- Unchanged 100,000 machine-data validation bound.\n- Reproducible per-lane instruction counts on one pinned commit.\n- A genuinely nonvacuous forgery regression on **both evaluators**, proving forged packets neither succeed nor execute the private body.\n- No raw consumer-machine serialization on budget exhaustion.\n\n**Verdict:** diagnostic round accepted; harness defect confirmed as test-side; uniform 4M approved subject to the landing checks above."}
